findings.body:
`_, _ = w.Write(b)` only acknowledges the return values so the compiler/linter stops complaining; it does not handle them. If `Write` returns a non-nil error or a short write, `Save` still reports success and callers cannot recover or surface the failure.

Propagate the error (and treat a short write as failure):

```go
func Save(w Writer, b []byte) error {
	n, err := w.Write(b)
	if err != nil {
		return err
	}
	if n < len(b) {
		return io.ErrShortWrite
	}
	return nil
}
```

As written, this does not address a review comment that asked to handle `Write` results.
